# GammaOS zram + block swap fstab for the RG DS Plus (microSD boot).
# Activated by init.rk30board.rc at boot-complete:
#   swapon_all /vendor/etc/fstab_swap.ext${vendor.ext_ram}
# with vendor.ext_ram=1024 and persist.sys.zram_enabled=1 (both in build.prop).
#
# Swap tiers, in priority order (higher swapprio = filled first):
#   1. zram0  (swapprio=2) - lz4-compressed RAM swap. comp_algorithm lz4 is set in
#      init.rk356x.rc. disksize 384MB with NO mem_limit: the kernel only falls over to
#      the next swap device when this one runs out of SLOTS, never when a RAM cap is
#      hit (a capped zram fails the write instead and the system thrashes in place while
#      the card swap sits empty, seen 2026-09-26 with 350MB of incompressible game data).
#      So the logical size IS the RAM budget: at most 384MB of RAM if every page is
#      incompressible, about half that for ordinary app memory, and once the slots are
#      used the overflow goes to the card below.
#   2. swap   (swapprio=1) - the dedicated 2GB block swap partition (GPT label 'swap',
#      /dev/block/by-name/swap). fs_mgr runs mkswap on it at every swapon_all, so it
#      needs no pre-formatting in the image. `wait` lets the by-name symlink settle.
#<src>                    <mnt_point>   <type>   <mnt_flags>   <fs_mgr_flags>
/dev/block/zram0          none          swap     defaults      zramsize=402653184,swapprio=2
/dev/block/by-name/swap   none          swap     defaults      swapprio=1,wait
